      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "This is not a generic electronic double bill. In a Space Outta Dub takes the material of Nightmares On Wax's In a Space Outta Sound and lets Adrian Sherwood dismantle and rebuild it twenty years later, so putting both artists into the same DUB SESSIONS room makes production language itself — sub-bass, echo, negative space and sound-system logic — the subject of the night. SILENT POETS' special dub ensemble adds a real Japanese lineage to the bill rather than functioning as arbitrary support.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room for this if dub, sound-system culture and electronic groove are part of the Tokyo thread. O-EAST gives the collaboration a strong Tokyo setting, while the same bill in Osaka the next night means there is useful flexibility rather than a reason to reorganize the larger Japan trip around this one date.",
